<p><code style="font-family:Consolas,'Courier New',monospace;background:#f2f2f2;padding:1px 4px;">OK</code> means the client accepted the request. It does not confirm the scan or evaluation finished successfully, so check the device 30 to 60 minutes later:</p>
<ol>
  <li>Open Control Panel &gt; <strong>Configuration Manager</strong> &gt; <strong>Actions</strong>. A recovered client lists a full set of actions, not just one or two.</li>
  <li>Open <strong>Software Center</strong> and confirm updates and applications are listed and can download.</li>
  <li>Open <code style="font-family:Consolas,'Courier New',monospace;background:#f2f2f2;padding:1px 4px;">C:\Windows\CCM\Logs\PolicyAgent.log</code> and confirm there are no new signature or hash errors after the time you ran the script.</li>
</ol>
<p>If the device has not recovered after 60 minutes, go to Option 2.</p>

<h2 style="font-size:20px;margin:32px 0 8px 0;padding-bottom:4px;border-bottom:1px solid #cccccc;text-align:left;">Option 2: Reinstall the client</h2>
<p>Use this when Option 1 fails, or when the device still cannot get software updates or communicate with the site an hour after a successful reset. A clean reinstall removes the client and everything it holds locally, then installs it fresh.</p>

<h3 style="font-size:16px;margin:24px 0 8px 0;text-align:left;">Before you start</h3>
<p>The reinstall is run from the MECM console on COR TSP, so nothing needs to be run on the device itself. You need access to the console and rights to install clients. The device must be powered on and connected to the network.</p>

<h3 style="font-size:16px;margin:24px 0 8px 0;text-align:left;">Steps</h3>
<ol>
  <li>Sign in to COR TSP and open the <strong>Configuration Manager console</strong>.</li>
  <li>Go to <strong>Assets and Compliance</strong> &gt; <strong>Devices</strong>.</li>
  <li>Type the device name in the search box and press Enter.</li>
  <li>Confirm you have the right device. If the name appears more than once, choose the record with the most recent activity.</li>
  <li>Right-click the device and select <strong>Install Client</strong>.</li>
  <li>Select <strong>Next</strong> on the first page of the wizard.</li>
  <li>On the <strong>Installation Options</strong> page, tick both of these:
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Always install the client software</strong></li>
      <li><strong>Uninstall existing Configuration Manager client before the client is installed</strong></li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li>If asked, select <strong>Install the client software from a specified site</strong> and choose your site.</li>
  <li>Select <strong>Next</strong>, <strong>Next</strong>, then <strong>Close</strong>.</li>
  <li>Wait 20 to 30 minutes, then refresh the device in the console. A successful reinstall shows <strong>Client: Yes</strong>, <strong>Client Activity: Active</strong> and a current policy request time.</li>
  <li>On the device, repeat the three checks in "Check the result". You do not need to run the Option 1 script afterwards.</li>
</ol>
<p>Notes:</p>
<ul>
  <li>The uninstall option is what clears the out-of-date policy. Without it, the client is repaired in place and the problem can remain.</li>
  <li>If the uninstall option is not shown in the wizard, stop and escalate.</li>
  <li>The uninstall can clear the client's download cache, so content already downloaded will be fetched again.</li>
  <li>If the device has not changed in the console after 60 minutes, escalate. The push may not have reached the device.</li>
</ul>

<h2 style="font-size:20px;margin:32px 0 8px 0;padding-bottom:4px;border-bottom:1px solid #cccccc;text-align:left;">Escalation</h2>
<p>If the device is still not working after Option 2, raise a DSMS ticket to <span style="background:#fff3cd;border:1px solid #e0c060;padding:1px 4px;">[ASSIGNMENT GROUP TO BE CONFIRMED]</span> and include:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Device name and location.</li>
  <li>Date and time each option was attempted.</li>
  <li>The output line from the Option 1 script.</li>
  <li>The symptoms still present.</li>
  <li>Copies of these logs:
    <ul>
      <li><code style="font-family:Consolas,'Courier New',monospace;background:#f2f2f2;padding:1px 4px;">C:\Windows\CCM\Logs\PolicyAgent.log</code></li>
      <li><code style="font-family:Consolas,'Courier New',monospace;background:#f2f2f2;padding:1px 4px;">C:\Windows\CCM\Logs\ClientIDManagerStartup.log</code></li>
      <li><code style="font-family:Consolas,'Courier New',monospace;background:#f2f2f2;padding:1px 4px;">C:\Windows\CCM\Logs\LocationServices.log</code></li>
      <li><code style="font-family:Consolas,'Courier New',monospace;background:#f2f2f2;padding:1px 4px;">C:\Windows\CCM\Logs\CcmMessaging.log</code></li>
      <li><code style="font-family:Consolas,'Courier New',monospace;background:#f2f2f2;padding:1px 4px;">C:\Windows\ccmsetup\Logs\ccmsetup.log</code></li>
    </ul>
  </li>
</ul>
